WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.140
Hi! I'm Bluebold,

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.020
and I catch sentences breaking the law.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:07.800
Today's crime: two complete sentences,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.420
glued together with a comma.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.980
Here's the evidence.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.780
The lab closed,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.000
the students went home.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.760
Is that okay?

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:17.920
Let's test it.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.940
Find the subject and verb on the left.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.660
The lab, closed.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.280
Complete. On the right.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.840
The students, went.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.560
Also complete. Both sides could stand alone.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.680
Two complete sentences need a real connection.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.980
A period. A semicolon.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.020
Or a comma with a joining word,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.660
like and, or so.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.960
A comma alone is not enough.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.280
Your turn. The rain stopped,

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.700
we went outside.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.080
Legal, or illegal?

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.460
Go.

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.390
Illegal! Two complete thoughts,

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:56.390
and just a comma.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.270
Fix it with a semicolon,

00:00:58.270 --> 00:00:59.610
or a comma and so.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.370
Careful, though. A semicolon needs a complete sentence on

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:06.410
both sides. Because it rained,

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.550
we stayed in.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.650
Because it rained can't stand alone.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.470
So a semicolon there is wrong.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.030
A comma works here.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:15.790
The fast way:

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.590
before you look at the punctuation choices,

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.990
find the subject and verb on each side.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.530
And read the whole sentence,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:22.750
not just the underlined words.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.270
Two complete sides.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:29.190
Period. Semicolon. Or a comma and a joining word.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.050
Now hit Try this skill,

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.330
and go catch some criminals!
